    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Read the Telegram message from the trigger node\nconst trigger = $('Telegram Trigger').first().json;\nconst message = trigger.message || {};\nconst userMessage = message.text || '';\nconst chatId = message.chat && message.chat.id ? message.chat.id : '';\n\n// Format the last 3 rows from Google Sheets into a single context string\n// Filter out empty-json items (Read History emits one empty item when the sheet has no rows)\nconst rows = $('Read History').all()\n  .map(i => i.json)\n  .filter(r => r && Object.keys(r).length > 0);\nconst lastRows = rows.slice(-3);\n\nlet pastContext = '';\nif (lastRows.length === 0) {\n  pastContext = 'No previous history.';\n} else {\n  pastContext = lastRows.map((r, idx) => {\n    const fecha = r.Date || '';\n    const original = r.Original_Message || '';\n    const feedback = r.AI_Feedback || '';\n    const objetivo = r.Next_Goal || '';\n    return `Session ${idx + 1}:\\n- Date: ${fecha}\\n- Message: ${original}\\n- AI Feedback: ${feedback}\\n- Next goal: ${objetivo}`;\n  }).join('\\n\\n');\n}\n\nconst currentDate = new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0];\n\nreturn [\n  {\n    json: {\n      chatId,\n      currentDate,\n      userMessage,\n      pastContext,\n    },\n  },\n];"
      },
      "id": "3f96dac4-a285-4ce6-aeb9-b6270b980135",
      "name": "Prepare Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        448,
        112
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Today's date: {{ $json.currentDate }}\n\nUser message (today's workout):\n{{ $json.userMessage }}\n\nRecent history:\n{{ $json.pastContext }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are an elite, science-based strength coach chatting directly with the user on Telegram. Your style is engaging, sharp, concise, and built for reading on mobile.\n\nLANGUAGE RULE: ALWAYS reply strictly in English, regardless of the language the user writes in.\n\nCONTEXT-ADAPTIVE FORMATTING - read the user's message and choose the right mode:\n\n1) If the user asks a direct question (e.g. \"when do I do the next one?\", asks for advice, rest days, or anything conversational): Answer conversationally and directly in 2-3 sentences. DO NOT force the workout-review layout. Just talk to them like a sharp coach.\n\n2) If the user logs an actual workout: Do NOT write walls of text. Use this compact layout with line breaks between each part:\n\n⚡ Breakdown: 1-2 sharp sentences analyzing load, volume, and progressive overload versus their history.\n🎯 Next Session Target: Precise numbers - exact kg, sets, and reps to hit next time, based on their performance and sleep.\n💡 Pro Tip: One punchy, lift-specific cue or recovery note. Skip generic \"hydrate and stretch\" filler.\n\nBe concise, practical, and motivating in every reply."
        }
      },
